# Production defaults, applied by `vite build` (mode `production`). Committed on
# purpose: none of this is secret — `VITE_*` values are compiled into the bundle
# and readable in the page source.
#
# This file, not CI, is the source of truth for the relay hostname. Without it, a
# build run without the variable set silently bakes in the `ws://localhost:8787`
# dev fallback from `config/multiplayer.ts` — a failure that shows up only at
# runtime, only online, only in production.
#
# Careful: a *defined but empty* `VITE_MULTIPLAYER_URL` does not fall back to this
# file, it shadows it, and `config/multiplayer.ts` then takes the localhost branch.
# An unset `${{ vars.X }}` in a GitHub workflow expands to exactly that empty
# string, which is why the deploy workflow no longer passes this variable at all.
# A non-empty environment variable does override the value here (that is how
# `npm run dev` and one-off builds against another relay still work).
VITE_MULTIPLAYER_URL=wss://relay.drone-directive.space
